WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.345 --> 00:00:19.949
Mary she had to answer Colin's questions about the secret garden, but she didn't want to.

2
00:00:19.969 --> 00:00:22.409
"Your father hated the garden.

3
00:00:22.829 --> 00:00:25.150
He locked the door," she said nervously.

4
00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.091
"No one knew where he buried the key."

5
00:00:29.111 --> 00:00:30.431
"What sort of garden is it?"

6
00:00:30.792 --> 00:00:32.032
Colin asked eagerly.

7
00:00:33.628 --> 00:00:38.112
"No one has been allowed to go inside for ten years," Mary said carefully.

8
00:00:39.253 --> 00:00:40.835
But it was too late to be careful.

9
00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:42.896
Colin was just like Mary.

10
00:00:44.017 --> 00:00:45.979
He'd had nothing to think about for years.

11
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.804
So the idea of a hidden garden interested him, just as it had interested her.

12
00:00:53.025 --> 00:00:54.787
He asked question after question.

13
00:00:55.247 --> 00:00:55.868
Where was it?

14
00:00:57.429 --> 00:00:58.550
Had she looked for the door?

15
00:00:59.051 --> 00:01:00.312
Had she asked the gardeners?

16
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.322
"I think they've been told not to answer questions about it," said Mary.

17
00:01:05.342 --> 00:01:07.743
"I would make them answer."

18
00:01:07.763 --> 00:01:09.383
"You would?"

19
00:01:09.924 --> 00:01:11.524
Mary began to feel frightened.

20
00:01:12.625 --> 00:01:15.926
If Colin could force people to answer, who knew what might happen!

21
00:01:15.946 --> 00:01:19.428
"I told you that everyone must please me.

22
00:01:20.648 --> 00:01:23.630
If I were to live, this place would someday belong to me.

23
00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:24.870
They all know that."

24
00:01:26.011 --> 00:01:28.672
In the past people had said that Mary was spoiled.

25
00:01:29.884 --> 00:01:31.445
She had never seen this in herself.

26
00:01:32.606 --> 00:01:35.087
But now she could see it quite plainly in Colin.

27
00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:38.229
He thought the whole world belonged to him.

28
00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:43.031
How mysterious he was and how coolly he spoke about dying.

29
00:01:43.051 --> 00:01:46.433
"Do you really think you're going to die?"

30
00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:52.456
Mary was curious about this, but she also wanted to distract him from the garden.

31
00:01:53.517 --> 00:01:55.898
"That's what people have been saying for a long time.

32
00:01:57.059 --> 00:01:58.700
My doctor is my father's cousin.

33
00:01:59.136 --> 00:02:00.017
He's quite poor.

34
00:02:01.117 --> 00:02:04.680
If I die, he'll have Misselthwaite Manor when my father is dead.

35
00:02:05.881 --> 00:02:07.242
I don't think he wants me to live."

36
00:02:07.262 --> 00:02:09.563
"Do you want to live?"

37
00:02:09.583 --> 00:02:13.926
"No." Colin sounded tired and angry.

38
00:02:13.946 --> 00:02:16.208
"But I don't want to die.

39
00:02:16.668 --> 00:02:19.970
When I'm ill, I lie here and think about dying until I cry."

40
00:02:19.991 --> 00:02:23.113
"I've heard you crying three times."

41
00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:25.474
"Let's talk about something else.

42
00:02:26.435 --> 00:02:27.656
Let's talk about that garden.

43
00:02:28.164 --> 00:02:28.984
Don't you want to see it?"

44
00:02:30.045 --> 00:02:31.485
"Yes," Mary said.

45
00:02:31.505 --> 00:02:34.486
"I want the key dug up.

46
00:02:35.046 --> 00:02:36.986
I'm going to make the servants open the door.

47
00:02:38.107 --> 00:02:40.087
I'll make them take me there in my wheelchair.

48
00:02:40.487 --> 00:02:41.628
And I will let you come too."

49
00:02:42.808 --> 00:02:44.428
Mary clutched her hands tightly.

50
00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:47.089
Everything would be ruined—everything!

51
00:02:48.149 --> 00:02:49.350
Dickon would never come back.

52
00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:53.731
She would never again feel as safe as a bird on her nest.

53
00:02:53.751 --> 00:02:56.612
"Oh, don't do that!"

54
00:02:57.132 --> 00:02:57.652
she cried.

55
00:02:58.760 --> 00:02:59.821
Colin stared at her.

56
00:03:00.421 --> 00:03:04.943
"Why?" "If you make them take you there, it'll never be a secret again.

57
00:03:05.983 --> 00:03:10.505
You see, if no one knows but us, and if we could find the hidden door, we could

58
00:03:10.525 --> 00:03:11.666
slip through it together."

59
00:03:12.846 --> 00:03:14.627
Mary's words came tumbling out.

60
00:03:16.548 --> 00:03:20.230
"We could play there every day and pretend we're birds and it's our nest.

61
00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:25.332
We could watch the flowers growing in the spring and see how many roses are alive.

62
00:03:26.432 --> 00:03:28.953
Don't you see how much nicer it would be if it were a secret?"

63
00:03:30.053 --> 00:03:32.014
There was an odd expression on his face.

64
00:03:32.034 --> 00:03:34.915
"I've never had a secret before."

65
00:03:34.935 --> 00:03:38.095
"Perhaps I could find the door.

66
00:03:39.056 --> 00:03:41.596
Then we could find some boy to take you out in your wheelchair."

67
00:03:41.616 --> 00:03:44.977
"I wouldn't mind fresh air in a secret garden."

68
00:03:45.418 --> 00:03:47.118
Colin suddenly looked pleased.

69
00:03:47.138 --> 00:03:49.439
"I'm going to show you something.

70
00:03:50.459 --> 00:03:52.660
Do you see that curtain hanging above the fireplace?

71
00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:53.560
Open it."

72
00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.361
Mary got up and pulled open the curtain.

73
00:03:59.442 --> 00:04:01.923
Underneath was a painting of a beautiful woman.

74
00:04:01.943 --> 00:04:03.964
"That's my mother.

75
00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.005
Sometimes I hate her for dying.

76
00:04:07.166 --> 00:04:10.007
If she were alive, maybe I wouldn't always be sick.

77
00:04:11.168 --> 00:04:12.909
And my father wouldn't hate to look at me.

78
00:04:13.409 --> 00:04:14.310
Draw the curtain again."

79
00:04:15.851 --> 00:04:19.833
Mary noticed that Colin's large, dark eyes were just like his mother's.

80
00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:23.335
She drew the curtain and sat down by the bed.

81
00:04:23.355 --> 00:04:25.216
"Why is the curtain closed?"

82
00:04:26.304 --> 00:04:27.845
"I don't like to see her looking at me.

83
00:04:28.805 --> 00:04:30.446
She smiles too much when I'm sick.

84
00:04:31.606 --> 00:04:34.568
Besides, she's mine, and I don't want everyone to see her."

85
00:04:36.028 --> 00:04:37.589
They were quiet for a few moments.

86
00:04:38.809 --> 00:04:39.490
"What would Mrs.

87
00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:41.871
Medlock do if she found out I was here?"

88
00:04:42.411 --> 00:04:43.091
asked Mary.

89
00:04:43.111 --> 00:04:45.212
"She'd do as I say.

90
00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:47.753
And I'd tell her that I want you to come every day.

91
00:04:48.153 --> 00:04:48.973
I'm glad you came."

92
00:04:48.994 --> 00:04:50.774
"So am I."

93
00:04:50.794 --> 00:04:54.756
"But for now I think I'll keep you a secret.

94
00:04:55.816 --> 00:04:57.378
I'll tell Martha when I want you to come.

95
00:04:57.798 --> 00:04:58.539
Do you know Martha?"

96
00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:00.380
Mary nodded.

97
00:05:00.881 --> 00:05:04.604
Now she understood Martha's troubled look when she asked about the crying.

98
00:05:04.624 --> 00:05:08.047
"Martha takes care of me when my nurse has the night off.

99
00:05:09.428 --> 00:05:11.229
She's sleeping in the next room right now."

100
00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:12.491
Colin yawned.

101
00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:14.933
"You're tired.

102
00:05:15.373 --> 00:05:16.414
I think I'd better go."

103
00:05:16.434 --> 00:05:19.336
"Oh, please don't go until I fall asleep."

104
00:05:20.537 --> 00:05:23.160
Somehow Mary felt sorry for this strange boy.

105
00:05:24.317 --> 00:05:26.763
So she sang softly until he fell asleep.

106
00:05:27.925 --> 00:05:30.331
Then she picked up her candle and crept away.
